{"parentUuid":"6e236011-6022-4891-9a1c-3e95188e2410","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d3c558b8-5926-493c-a40f-61e97a9f4b9c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BgUttb6yFMtCsprE4mkQ9j","type":"tool_result","content":"120\t`manual` injection mode is out of scope for beta.\n121\t\n122\t---\n123\t\n124\t## 3. Storage Architecture\n125\t\n126\t### Local storage: SQLite\n127\t\n128\tAll reads and writes go through `.entire/memory-loop.db` (WAL mode, busy timeout, retry-once on contention).\n129\t\n130\tTables:\n131\t\n132\t- `schema_version`\n133\t- `memories` — lessons\n134\t- `experiences` — experiences\n135\t- `memory_history` — lifecycle events (polymorphic: type + id columns reference either table)\n136\t- `injection_logs` — per-turn record of what was selected and why\n137\t- `refresh_history` — per-refresh counts (generated, activated, candidates, filtered, deduped, skipped)\n138\t- `analysis_cache` — cached `CheckpointAnalysis` keyed by `(checkpoint_id, repo_id)`\n139\t\n140\tSchema shape for lessons (unchanged from the prior memory-loop design):\n141\t\n142\t```sql\n143\tmemories (\n144\t  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n145\t  kind TEXT NOT NULL,\n146\t  summary TEXT NOT NULL,\n147\t  decisions_json TEXT NOT NULL,\n148\t  failed_approaches_json TEXT NOT NULL,\n149\t  warnings_json TEXT NOT NULL,\n150\t  error_signatures_json TEXT NOT NULL,\n151\t  cause_chain_json TEXT NOT NULL,\n152\t  file_dependencies_json TEXT NOT NULL,\n153\t  key_insights_json TEXT NOT NULL,\n154\t  scope_kind TEXT NOT NULL,\n155\t  scope_value TEXT,\n156\t  status TEXT NOT NULL,\n157\t  origin TEXT NOT NULL,\n158\t  fingerprint TEXT NOT NULL,\n159\t  confidence TEXT,\n160\t  strength INTEGER,\n161\t  source_signal TEXT,\n162\t  outcome TEXT DEFAULT 'neutral',\n163\t  inject_count INTEGER DEFAULT 0,\n164\t  source_experience_ids_json TEXT,   -- set only for derived lessons\n165\t  derived_from_origin TEXT,           -- 'experience' | NULL\n166\t  owner_id TEXT,                      -- durable identifier for personal scope\n167\t  created_at TEXT NOT NULL,\n168\t  updated_at TEXT NOT NULL,\n169\t  last_injected_at TEXT\n170\t)\n171\t```\n172\t\n173\tSchema shape for experiences:\n174\t\n175\t```sql\n176\texperiences (\n177\t  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n178\t  task_class TEXT NOT NULL,           -- from controlled vocabulary\n179\t  scope_kind TEXT NOT NULL,\n180\t  scope_value TEXT,\n181\t  status TEXT NOT NULL,\n182\t  origin TEXT NOT NULL,\n183\t  goal_summary TEXT NOT NULL,\n184\t  attempted_steps_json TEXT NOT NULL,\n185\t  successful_steps_json TEXT NOT NULL,\n186\t  failed_steps_json TEXT NOT NULL,\n187\t  tool_patterns_json TEXT NOT NULL,\n188\t  trigger_signals_json TEXT NOT NULL,\n189\t  initial_context_json TEXT NOT NULL,\n190\t  file_dependencies_json TEXT NOT NULL,   -- required, array, empty permitted\n191\t  error_signatures_json TEXT NOT NULL,    -- required, array, empty permitted\n192\t  source_signal TEXT NOT NULL,             -- required, empty string permitted\n193\t  outcome TEXT NOT NULL,                   -- 'success', 'partial', 'failed'\n194\t  fingerprint TEXT NOT NULL,\n195\t  source_checkpoint_ids_json TEXT NOT NULL,\n196\t  source_session_ids_json TEXT NOT NULL,\n197\t  confidence TEXT,\n198\t  strength INTEGER,\n199\t  inject_count INTEGER DEFAULT 0,\n200\t  owner_id TEXT,\n201\t  sanitizer_warnings_json TEXT,            -- fields that triggered sanitizer rewrites\n202\t  created_at TEXT NOT NULL,\n203\t  updated_at TEXT NOT NULL,\n204\t  last_injected_at TEXT\n205\t)\n206\t```\n207\t\n208\t**Controlled `task_class` vocabulary** (extensible via code, not via settings):\n209\t\n210\t```\n211\tbuild_failure, integration_test_failure, flaky_test, repo_setup,\n212\tauth_bug, migration, refactor, debugging, unclassified\n213\t```\n214\t\n215\t`unclassified` is a mandatory fallback slot so the validator can always assign a value. Extraction output that does not match the vocabulary is rewritten to `unclassified` with a telemetry note.\n216\t\n217\t### Storage rules\n218\t\n219\t- Versioned migrations. No `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS`-only paths.\n220\t- Every JSON column has a corresponding Go struct with a schema version tag.\n221\t- Indexes: `(status)`, `(scope_kind, scope_value)`, `(fingerprint)`, `(owner_id)`, `(analysis_cache: repo_id, fetched_at)`.\n222\t- No hard row cap in beta; growth is monitored.\n223\t\n224\t### Analysis cache\n225\t\n226\t`analysis_cache` caches `CheckpointAnalysis` from the entire.io API:\n227\t\n228\t- Fresh if `fetched_at` is within 24 hours.\n229\t- Cache key includes `content_hash`; a changed hash replaces the row and re-runs generation.\n230\t- `generator_version` is a monotonically-increasing constant; a bump forces re-generation against unchanged content.\n231\t- Degraded mode: within 48 hours of `fetched_at`, stale entries may still be used for memory generation. Older than 48 hours, they are skipped. Refresh reports how many were skipped.\n232\t- Rows older than 90 days are eligible for eviction.\n233\t\n234\t### Remote storage\n235\t\n236\tRepo-scoped lessons sync via a code-owner-selected backend (checkpoint branch or EntireDB — see Section 11 open questions). **Experiences do not sync in beta** regardless of `scope_kind`, even if repo-scoped. Sync of procedural traces requires a separate redaction design; until then, experiences are local-only.\n237\t\n238\t---\n239\t\n240\t## 4. Generation\n241\t\n242\t### Single refresh, two extraction targets\n243\t\n244\tBoth memory types come from the same refresh pass:\n245\t\n246\t```\n247\tentire memory-loop refresh\n248\t\n249\t  Identify recent checkpoints (synced + local)\n250\t          │\n251\t          ├─ synced: GET /analysis?checkpoint_id&repo_id\n252\t          │\n253\t          └─ unsynced: POST /analysis with scoped transcript\n254\t          │\n255\t          ▼\n256\t  Cache CheckpointAnalysis (skip unchanged)\n257\t          │\n258\t          ├─ Lesson extractor  ─> lesson candidates\n259\t          └─ Experience extractor ─> experience candidates\n260\t          │\n261\t          ▼\n262\t  Preset admission gate\n263\t          │\n264\t          ▼\n265\t  Dedup by fingerprint\n266\t          │\n267\t          ▼\n268\t  Reconcile with existing records\n269\t          │\n270\t          ▼\n271\t  Apply activation policy and write\n272\t```\n273\t\n274\tRefresh is manual only in beta. Auto-refresh is deferred until generation quality is trusted.\n275\t\n276\t### Lesson extraction\n277\t\n278\tLesson extraction runs over `CheckpointAnalysis` alone. It is the faster path and is the default extraction target for every eligible checkpoint.\n279\t\n280\tAdmission by preset:\n281\t\n282\t- `flexible` — `summary` plus any lower-signal field\n283\t- `balanced` (default) — `summary` plus at least one populated high-signal field\n284\t- `strict` — `summary` plus at least two populated high-signal fields\n285\t\n286\tGeneric records (vague advice, one-line \"be careful\" text) are rejected.\n287\t\n288\t### Experience extraction\n289\t\n290\tExperience extraction needs ordered trajectory data, which `CheckpointAnalysis` does not reliably emit. Dual-input source model:\n291\t\n292\t- `CheckpointAnalysis` for candidate selection, provenance, and stable normalized fields (`source_signal`, `file_dependencies`, `error_signatures`, `task_class`)\n293\t- Ordered action evidence, from either:\n294\t  1. A future `CheckpointAnalysis` extension that emits ordered action summaries (preferred)\n295\t  2. A local transcript reader that extracts ordered steps from checkpoint-scoped transcript files (fallback)\n296\t\n297\tIf neither source is available for a checkpoint, it is ineligible and counted separately in refresh output as `skipped_no_trajectory_data`.\n298\t\n299\t**Transcript ingress redaction**, required before the local transcript reader ships:\n300\t\n301\t- Transcripts pass through a local redactor **before** entering any LLM prompt.\n302\t- Redactor strips common secret shapes: AWS keys, GitHub tokens, JWTs, OpenAI `sk-` keys, PEM blocks, high-entropy strings above a length floor.\n303\t- Redaction is deterministic and local — no LLM involvement at this stage.\n304\t- PR 7 acceptance criteria include a planted-secret corpus with zero-leak output.\n305\t- Refresh reports the volume of transcript text egressed per run.\n306\t\n307\tPrefer successful recovery sequences, repeated troubleshooting flows, multi-step repair patterns, and task classes with strong file or error-signature locality. Reject single-step generic advice, vague recommendations, episodes with no reusable sequence.\n308\t\n309\t### Sanitization (both extractors)\n310\t\n311\tBefore writing any LLM-generated string field to storage:\n312\t\n313\t- Strip role markers (`system:`, `assistant:`, `user:`)\n314\t- Strip fenced instruction blocks\n315\t- Strip XML-like tag openers that resemble system-prompt delimiters\n316\t- Strip leading imperatives paired with known tool or command verbs matching the deny-list\n317\t\n318\tSanitization runs at ingress, not at render time. Any field that required a rewrite is recorded in `sanitizer_warnings_json` so the TUI reviewer sees it.\n319\t"}]},"uuid":"c532eefe-e9f9-4f8f-ad81-c33ad89eace0","timestamp":"2026-04-28T21:35:01.303Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/alisha/.superset/worktrees/cli/agent-improvements/docs/plans/2026-04-16-agent-memory-design.md","content":"`manual` injection mode is out of scope for beta.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Storage Architecture\n\n### Local storage: SQLite\n\nAll reads and writes go through `.entire/memory-loop.db` (WAL mode, busy timeout, retry-once on contention).\n\nTables:\n\n- `schema_version`\n- `memories` — lessons\n- `experiences` — experiences\n- `memory_history` — lifecycle events (polymorphic: type + id columns reference either table)\n- `injection_logs` — per-turn record of what was selected and why\n- `refresh_history` — per-refresh counts (generated, activated, candidates, filtered, deduped, skipped)\n- `analysis_cache` — cached `CheckpointAnalysis` keyed by `(checkpoint_id, repo_id)`\n\nSchema shape for lessons (unchanged from the prior memory-loop design):\n\n```sql\nmemories (\n  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n  kind TEXT NOT NULL,\n  summary TEXT NOT NULL,\n  decisions_json TEXT NOT NULL,\n  failed_approaches_json TEXT NOT NULL,\n  warnings_json TEXT NOT NULL,\n  error_signatures_json TEXT NOT NULL,\n  cause_chain_json TEXT NOT NULL,\n  file_dependencies_json TEXT NOT NULL,\n  key_insights_json TEXT NOT NULL,\n  scope_kind TEXT NOT NULL,\n  scope_value TEXT,\n  status TEXT NOT NULL,\n  origin TEXT NOT NULL,\n  fingerprint TEXT NOT NULL,\n  confidence TEXT,\n  strength INTEGER,\n  source_signal TEXT,\n  outcome TEXT DEFAULT 'neutral',\n  inject_count INTEGER DEFAULT 0,\n  source_experience_ids_json TEXT,   -- set only for derived lessons\n  derived_from_origin TEXT,           -- 'experience' | NULL\n  owner_id TEXT,                      -- durable identifier for personal scope\n  created_at TEXT NOT NULL,\n  updated_at TEXT NOT NULL,\n  last_injected_at TEXT\n)\n```\n\nSchema shape for experiences:\n\n```sql\nexperiences (\n  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n  task_class TEXT NOT NULL,           -- from controlled vocabulary\n  scope_kind TEXT NOT NULL,\n  scope_value TEXT,\n  status TEXT NOT NULL,\n  origin TEXT NOT NULL,\n  goal_summary TEXT NOT NULL,\n  attempted_steps_json TEXT NOT NULL,\n  successful_steps_json TEXT NOT NULL,\n  failed_steps_json TEXT NOT NULL,\n  tool_patterns_json TEXT NOT NULL,\n  trigger_signals_json TEXT NOT NULL,\n  initial_context_json TEXT NOT NULL,\n  file_dependencies_json TEXT NOT NULL,   -- required, array, empty permitted\n  error_signatures_json TEXT NOT NULL,    -- required, array, empty permitted\n  source_signal TEXT NOT NULL,             -- required, empty string permitted\n  outcome TEXT NOT NULL,                   -- 'success', 'partial', 'failed'\n  fingerprint TEXT NOT NULL,\n  source_checkpoint_ids_json TEXT NOT NULL,\n  source_session_ids_json TEXT NOT NULL,\n  confidence TEXT,\n  strength INTEGER,\n  inject_count INTEGER DEFAULT 0,\n  owner_id TEXT,\n  sanitizer_warnings_json TEXT,            -- fields that triggered sanitizer rewrites\n  created_at TEXT NOT NULL,\n  updated_at TEXT NOT NULL,\n  last_injected_at TEXT\n)\n```\n\n**Controlled `task_class` vocabulary** (extensible via code, not via settings):\n\n```\nbuild_failure, integration_test_failure, flaky_test, repo_setup,\nauth_bug, migration, refactor, debugging, unclassified\n```\n\n`unclassified` is a mandatory fallback slot so the validator can always assign a value. Extraction output that does not match the vocabulary is rewritten to `unclassified` with a telemetry note.\n\n### Storage rules\n\n- Versioned migrations. No `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS`-only paths.\n- Every JSON column has a corresponding Go struct with a schema version tag.\n- Indexes: `(status)`, `(scope_kind, scope_value)`, `(fingerprint)`, `(owner_id)`, `(analysis_cache: repo_id, fetched_at)`.\n- No hard row cap in beta; growth is monitored.\n\n### Analysis cache\n\n`analysis_cache` caches `CheckpointAnalysis` from the entire.io API:\n\n- Fresh if `fetched_at` is within 24 hours.\n- Cache key includes `content_hash`; a changed hash replaces the row and re-runs generation.\n- `generator_version` is a monotonically-increasing constant; a bump forces re-generation against unchanged content.\n- Degraded mode: within 48 hours of `fetched_at`, stale entries may still be used for memory generation. Older than 48 hours, they are skipped. Refresh reports how many were skipped.\n- Rows older than 90 days are eligible for eviction.\n\n### Remote storage\n\nRepo-scoped lessons sync via a code-owner-selected backend (checkpoint branch or EntireDB — see Section 11 open questions). **Experiences do not sync in beta** regardless of `scope_kind`, even if repo-scoped. Sync of procedural traces requires a separate redaction design; until then, experiences are local-only.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Generation\n\n### Single refresh, two extraction targets\n\nBoth memory types come from the same refresh pass:\n\n```\nentire memory-loop refresh\n\n  Identify recent checkpoints (synced + local)\n          │\n          ├─ synced: GET /analysis?checkpoint_id&repo_id\n          │\n          └─ unsynced: POST /analysis with scoped transcript\n          │\n          ▼\n  Cache CheckpointAnalysis (skip unchanged)\n          │\n          ├─ Lesson extractor  ─> lesson candidates\n          └─ Experience extractor ─> experience candidates\n          │\n          ▼\n  Preset admission gate\n          │\n          ▼\n  Dedup by fingerprint\n          │\n          ▼\n  Reconcile with existing records\n          │\n          ▼\n  Apply activation policy and write\n```\n\nRefresh is manual only in beta. Auto-refresh is deferred until generation quality is trusted.\n\n### Lesson extraction\n\nLesson extraction runs over `CheckpointAnalysis` alone. It is the faster path and is the default extraction target for every eligible checkpoint.\n\nAdmission by preset:\n\n- `flexible` — `summary` plus any lower-signal field\n- `balanced` (default) — `summary` plus at least one populated high-signal field\n- `strict` — `summary` plus at least two populated high-signal fields\n\nGeneric records (vague advice, one-line \"be careful\" text) are rejected.\n\n### Experience extraction\n\nExperience extraction needs ordered trajectory data, which `CheckpointAnalysis` does not reliably emit. Dual-input source model:\n\n- `CheckpointAnalysis` for candidate selection, provenance, and stable normalized fields (`source_signal`, `file_dependencies`, `error_signatures`, `task_class`)\n- Ordered action evidence, from either:\n  1. A future `CheckpointAnalysis` extension that emits ordered action summaries (preferred)\n  2. A local transcript reader that extracts ordered steps from checkpoint-scoped transcript files (fallback)\n\nIf neither source is available for a checkpoint, it is ineligible and counted separately in refresh output as `skipped_no_trajectory_data`.\n\n**Transcript ingress redaction**, required before the local transcript reader ships:\n\n- Transcripts pass through a local redactor **before** entering any LLM prompt.\n- Redactor strips common secret shapes: AWS keys, GitHub tokens, JWTs, OpenAI `sk-` keys, PEM blocks, high-entropy strings above a length floor.\n- Redaction is deterministic and local — no LLM involvement at this stage.\n- PR 7 acceptance criteria include a planted-secret corpus with zero-leak output.\n- Refresh reports the volume of transcript text egressed per run.\n\nPrefer successful recovery sequences, repeated troubleshooting flows, multi-step repair patterns, and task classes with strong file or error-signature locality. Reject single-step generic advice, vague recommendations, episodes with no reusable sequence.\n\n### Sanitization (both extractors)\n\nBefore writing any LLM-generated string field to storage:\n\n- Strip role markers (`system:`, `assistant:`, `user:`)\n- Strip fenced instruction blocks\n- Strip XML-like tag openers that resemble system-prompt delimiters\n- Strip leading imperatives paired with known tool or command verbs matching the deny-list\n\nSanitization runs at ingress, not at render time. Any field that required a rewrite is recorded in `sanitizer_warnings_json` so the TUI reviewer sees it.\n","numLines":200,"startLine":120,"totalLines":751}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6e236011-6022-4891-9a1c-3e95188e2410","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-cli","cwd":"/Users/alisha/.superset/worktrees/cli/agent-improvements","sessionId":"5eec25c8-61b1-4881-bbd6-91e8595e790c","version":"2.1.121","gitBranch":"agent-improvements"}
{"parentUuid":"c532eefe-e9f9-4f8f-ad81-c33ad89eace0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_0116e54wYNQoQUuHYZqL7iS4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01N9oaRN9cniFFpgKWEmer5B","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/alisha/.superset/worktrees/cli/agent-improvements/docs/plans/2026-04-16-agent-memory-design.md","offset":320,"limit":220},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3894,"cache_read_input_tokens":90176,"output_tokens":156,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3894,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":156,"cache_read_input_tokens":90176,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3894,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3894},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CaWtSyxYLcoduuspAMVQC","type":"assistant","uuid":"1491a18a-8845-43c8-9db2-090f57f78a08","timestamp":"2026-04-28T21:35:04.234Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-cli","cwd":"/Users/alisha/.superset/worktrees/cli/agent-improvements","sessionId":"5eec25c8-61b1-4881-bbd6-91e8595e790c","version":"2.1.121","gitBranch":"agent-improvements"}
{"parentUuid":"1491a18a-8845-43c8-9db2-090f57f78a08","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d3c558b8-5926-493c-a40f-61e97a9f4b9c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01N9oaRN9cniFFpgKWEmer5B","type":"tool_result","content":"320\t### Fingerprinting\n321\t\n322\tFingerprint is load-bearing for dedup and suppression, so it must be deterministic and resistant to NULL-collapse.\n323\t\n324\t**Lesson fingerprint** — sha256 of canonical JSON over:\n325\t\n326\t- `kind`\n327\t- normalized `failed_approaches[]`\n328\t- normalized `error_signatures[]`\n329\t- normalized `cause_chain[]`\n330\t- normalized `file_dependencies[]`\n331\t- `scope_kind`, `scope_value`\n332\t\n333\t**Experience fingerprint** — sha256 of canonical JSON over:\n334\t\n335\t- `task_class` (from controlled vocabulary, including the mandatory `unclassified` fallback)\n336\t- sorted `file_dependencies[]` (empty array permitted, distinct from NULL)\n337\t- sorted `error_signatures[]` (empty array permitted, distinct from NULL)\n338\t- normalized `source_signal` (empty string permitted, distinct from NULL)\n339\t- `scope_kind`, `scope_value`\n340\t\n341\tExplicit exclusions:\n342\t\n343\t- LLM-generated prose fields (`summary`, `goal_summary`, step lists, `trigger_signals`) — non-deterministic.\n344\t- `source_checkpoint_ids` and `source_session_ids` — evidence, not identity.\n345\t\n346\t**Required fields are all fingerprint inputs.** The validator rejects records where any fingerprint input is NULL so null-profile records never collide.\n347\t\n348\tPR 1 regression tests:\n349\t\n350\t1. **Determinism** — two independent extraction runs over identical source inputs produce byte-identical fingerprints, including across a simulated analyzer-version bump.\n351\t2. **NULL-collapse prevention** — two records with different prose but both missing every fingerprint input are rejected by the validator (preferred) or produce distinct fingerprints. They never share a hash.\n352\t3. **Scope isolation** — a `me`-scoped record and a `repo`-scoped record with otherwise identical fingerprint inputs produce distinct fingerprints.\n353\t\n354\t### API authorization and cache binding\n355\t\n356\t- Authorization is server-side. Every API request verifies the authenticated user has access to the repo identified in the request.\n357\t- `GET /analysis?checkpoint_id=<id>&repo_id=<id>` for synced checkpoints.\n358\t- `POST /analysis` with a scoped payload for unsynced checkpoints.\n359\t- The API response must include `checkpoint_id`, `repo_id`, and `schema_version` matching the request; mismatches are discarded and logged.\n360\t- `403` → log the denied repo, continue to the next checkpoint.\n361\t- Local `analysis_cache` is keyed by `(checkpoint_id, repo_id)` and verified against the current repo before use.\n362\t\n363\t---\n364\t\n365\t## 5. Injection\n366\t\n367\t### Hot-path contract\n368\t\n369\t```\n370\tTurnStart\n371\t  │\n372\t  ▼\n373\tmode == off?  ──yes──> return no-op\n374\t  │ no\n375\t  ▼\n376\tScore active lessons\n377\t  │\n378\t  ▼\n379\tSelect top N under byte budget  ──> lesson bundle\n380\t  │\n381\t  ▼\n382\tExperience layer enabled?  ──no──> inject lesson bundle\n383\t  │ yes\n384\t  ▼\n385\tClassify procedural need (local, no LLM)\n386\t  │\n387\t  ▼\n388\tProcedural need high?  ──no──> inject lesson bundle\n389\t  │ yes\n390\t  ▼\n391\tFetch top-2 active experiences\n392\t  │\n393\t  ▼\n394\tActive lesson covers same task_class or ≥50% file overlap?\n395\t  ──yes──> drop experience; inject lessons only\n396\t  │ no\n397\t  ▼\n398\tInject lesson bundle + <prior-solve-path> block\n399\t  │\n400\t  ▼\n401\tLog injection (selected IDs, scores, fallbacks)\n402\t```\n403\t\n404\tTarget: total injection path under 50 ms, including experience retrieval. Log a warning if exceeded. A runtime circuit breaker reverts to lesson-only if the experience layer is over budget, and the fallback is surfaced in `entire status`.\n405\t\n406\t### Scoring\n407\t\n408\tScoring uses structured fields only. `summary` and `goal_summary` are not scoring inputs.\n409\t\n410\t**Lesson primary signals:** `error_signatures[]`, `file_dependencies[]`, `failed_approaches[]`, `cause_chain[]`\n411\t**Lesson secondary signals:** `decisions[]`, `key_insights[]`, `warnings[]` (balanced/flexible only)\n412\t\n413\t**Experience retrieval signals:** `task_class` match, `file_dependencies[]` overlap, `error_signatures[]` overlap, recency, outcome bonus\n414\t\n415\tAdditional factors for both:\n416\t\n417\t- Embedding similarity in `balanced`\n418\t- Outcome bonus (reinforced) and penalty (ineffective)\n419\t- Cooldown penalty for recently injected records\n420\t- Diversity across same-fingerprint records\n421\t\n422\tEmbedding fallback: if embeddings are unavailable, scoring falls back silently and records the fallback in `injection_logs.used_embedding_fallback`.\n423\t\n424\t### Procedural-need classifier\n425\t\n426\tRuns per turn, locally, with no new LLM calls. Inputs are already-computed signals:\n427\t\n428\t- Lesson scorer margin (weak lesson confidence → higher procedural need)\n429\t- File overlap strength across existing experiences\n430\t- Error-signature overlap strength\n431\t- Repeated failure-loop detection from session state\n432\t- Explicit task classification (debugging, migration, setup, repair, flaky tests)\n433\t\n434\tThe classifier output is a single real-valued score; a threshold (tunable via settings within a code-pinned floor) decides whether experience retrieval runs for this turn.\n435\t\n436\t### Injection form\n437\t\n438\tLessons are injected inline as structured guidance. Experiences are injected inside explicit delimiters so downstream token scanning can detect tampering:\n439\t\n440\t```\n441\t<prior-solve-path task-class=\"integration_test_failure\">\n442\tstep: Reproduce in isolated temp repo first\n443\tstep: Trace cwd-based git resolution before changing strategy logic\n444\tstep: Use testutil.InitRepo + seed commit + t.Chdir\n445\tavoid: Running lifecycle handlers from the real repo cwd\n446\t</prior-solve-path>\n447\t```\n448\t\n449\tThe TUI detail view shows the exact string that will be injected, after sanitization. Promotion to `active` is on that view — not on the raw stored record.\n450\t\n451\t### Kill switch\n452\t\n453\t`settings.ExperienceMemoryEnabled` toggles the experience layer at runtime. Default: off until PR 10 telemetry is clean. A separate `settings.MemoryLoopEnabled` toggles both layers. The kill switch is advertised in `entire status` and flipping it takes effect without a code change.\n454\t\n455\t---\n456\t\n457\t## 6. Governance and Review\n458\t\n459\t### Review surface\n460\t\n461\tTUI is the only review surface in beta. Two top-level lenses:\n462\t\n463\t- **Lessons** — list + detail, structured fields visible before promotion\n464\t- **Experiences** — list + detail, ordered steps visible, rendered injection form visible, `sanitizer_warnings_json` surfaced\n465\t\n466\tCross-links:\n467\t\n468\t- From a lesson detail: \"Derived from experiences\" when applicable\n469\t- From an experience detail: \"Related lessons from this experience\"\n470\t\n471\t### Governance actions (both types)\n472\t\n473\t`activate`, `suppress`, `unsuppress`, `archive`, `promote` (scope promotion), `demote` (auto-promoted experiences back to `candidate`).\n474\t\n475\t### Suppression and regeneration\n476\t\n477\tSuppression keys on `fingerprint + scope_kind + scope_value`. A suppressed record blocks regeneration for that exact fingerprint-in-scope combination, regardless of how the extractor rewrites the prose fields. Suppression is preserved indefinitely in beta.\n478\t\n479\t### Review forcing function\n480\t\n481\tCandidates that sit unreviewed are invisible to users unless they actively promote. To avoid a world where nothing gets promoted and injection never fires, PR 10 seeds experience injection with an **auto-promotion quality score**:\n482\t\n483\tAuto-promotion criteria (all must hold):\n484\t\n485\t- All fingerprint inputs present (by construction, since they are required)\n486\t- `outcome == 'success'`\n487\t- Ordered-trajectory source was available (not the `skipped_no_trajectory_data` path)\n488\t- Zero sanitizer warnings\n489\t- Dedup count ≥ 2 (the pattern has recurred)\n490\t\n491\tAuto-promoted experiences land as `active` with `origin = 'generated_auto_promoted'`. Reviewers can demote them. Telemetry distinguishes auto-promoted from human-promoted records so adoption can be measured honestly.\n492\t\n493\t---\n494\t\n495\t## 7. Deriving Lessons from Experiences\n496\t\n497\tRepeated experiences can synthesize or reinforce lessons. Unguarded derivation is a feedback loop (active lesson shapes a session → session produces an experience that echoes the lesson → echo reinforces the lesson). Derivation is therefore tightly gated.\n498\t\n499\t### Evidence independence\n500\t\n501\tDerivation requires all of:\n502\t\n503\t- At least `MinDerivationSessions` distinct source sessions (floor: **3**)\n504\t- Across at least `MinDerivationCheckpointBases` distinct checkpoint bases (floor: **2**)\n505\t- **Independence**: either (a) at least `MinDistinctOwnersOrBranches = 2` distinct `owner_id` values among source sessions, or (b) at least 2 distinct working branches with a minimum `MinSessionTimeSpan = 24h` wall-clock separation between the earliest and latest source session\n506\t\n507\tThe independence rule prevents a single user retrying the same bug three times from clearing the bar. Without it, \"3 distinct source sessions\" measures persistence-of-one-user, not evidence independence.\n508\t\n509\t### Code-pinned thresholds\n510\t\n511\t`MinDerivationSessions`, `MinDerivationCheckpointBases`, `MinDistinctOwnersOrBranches`, and `MinSessionTimeSpan` are pinned in code. Settings may **raise** these values. A settings value below the floor is rejected at load time and the floor is used instead.\n512\t\n513\tPR 12 includes a test that attempts to configure each threshold below its floor and asserts rejection.\n514\t\n515\t### Circular support\n516\t\n517\tA lesson cannot be reinforced by experiences whose **earliest source session turn timestamp** falls at or after the lesson's activation timestamp. The derivation job checks session turn timestamps, not experience `created_at`, because refresh can run long after a session ends.\n518\t\n519\t### Audit log\n520\t\n521\tEach derivation attempt is logged with inputs, thresholds in effect, and outcome (eligible/rejected). This is the audit trail for threshold tampering and circular-support misses.\n522\t\n523\t### Candidate status and linkage\n524\t\n525\t- Derived lessons always enter as `candidate`, even under `policy=auto`.\n526\t- Each derived lesson stores `source_experience_ids[]` so reviewers see evidence before promotion.\n527\t- The TUI shows both sides of the link.\n528\t\n529\t---\n530\t\n531\t## 8. Outcome Tracking\n532\t\n533\tOutcome tracking is unified across both memory types and answers: \"did this record make subsequent sessions better on the thing it was meant to help with?\"\n534\t\n535\t### Rules\n536\t\n537\t- Manual records are always `neutral` — no outcome is computed.\n538\t- Records with `inject_count < 3` remain `neutral`.\n539\t- After 3+ injections, compare post-injection sessions against the record's `source_signal`:"}]},"uuid":"96cdaf56-af7e-42fd-83ad-a272453445fb","timestamp":"2026-04-28T21:35:04.302Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/alisha/.superset/worktrees/cli/agent-improvements/docs/plans/2026-04-16-agent-memory-design.md","content":"### Fingerprinting\n\nFingerprint is load-bearing for dedup and suppression, so it must be deterministic and resistant to NULL-collapse.\n\n**Lesson fingerprint** — sha256 of canonical JSON over:\n\n- `kind`\n- normalized `failed_approaches[]`\n- normalized `error_signatures[]`\n- normalized `cause_chain[]`\n- normalized `file_dependenci