-path>` delimiters with labeled lines (`step:`, `avoid:`), not free-form bullets.\n571\t- **Review the rendered form** — the TUI detail view shows the exact injected string, including sanitizer output. Promotion is on that view.\n572\t- **Candidate default for manual experiences** — manual experiences enter as `candidate` so the rendered form can be reviewed once before it ships into sessions.\n573\t- **No experience sync in beta** — procedural traces are local-only regardless of `scope_kind`.\n574\t- **Kill switch** — runtime toggle to revert to lesson-only.\n575\t\n576\t---\n577\t\n578\t## 10. Rollout Plan\n579\t\n580\tVertical slices. Each PR delivers one working feature end-to-end.\n581\t\n582\t```\n583\tPR Dependency Graph\n584\t===================\n585\t\n586\t  PR 1:  Unified store + manual add (both types)\n587\t         │\n588\t         ▼\n589\t  PR 2:  Lifecycle + manual editing\n590\t         │\n591\t         ▼\n592\t  PR 3:  Lesson generation from CheckpointAnalysis\n593\t         │\n594\t         ▼\n595\t  PR 4:  Lesson injection + scoring\n596\t         │\n597\t         ▼\n598\t  PR 5:  Shared repo sync (lessons only)\n599\t         │\n600\t         ▼\n601\t  PR 6:  TUI review (lessons)\n602\t         │\n603\t         ▼\n604\t  PR 7:  Experience generation (ordered trajectory + redaction)\n605\t         │\n606\t         ▼\n607\t  PR 8:  TUI review (experiences) with rendered-form view\n608\t         │\n609\t         ▼\n610\t  PR 9:  Procedural-need classifier + shadow retrieval + telemetry\n611\t         │\n612\t         ▼\n613\t  PR 10: Experience injection (cohort + auto-promote seed)\n614\t         │\n615\t         ▼\n616\t  PR 11: Unified outcome tracking\n617\t         │\n618\t         ▼\n619\t  PR 12: Derive lessons from experiences\n620\t```\n621\t\n622\t### PR 1 — Unified store + manual add\n623\t\n624\t- SQLite setup, migrations, WAL mode\n625\t- `memories` and `experiences` tables\n626\t- Fingerprint computation for both types\n627\t- Validator that rejects records with NULL fingerprint inputs\n628\t- Manual add flow for both types\n629\t- List and detail views\n630\t- **Required tests**: fingerprint determinism, NULL-collapse prevention, scope isolation\n631\t\n632\t### PR 2 — Lifecycle + manual editing\n633\t\n634\t- `activate`, `suppress`, `unsuppress`, `archive`, `promote`, `demote` for both types\n635\t- `memory_history` table and event recording\n636\t- Manual edit flow (manual records only)\n637\t- Scope/status filtering in views\n638\t\n639\t### PR 3 — Lesson generation\n640\t\n641\t- Fetch `CheckpointAnalysis` from the entire.io API\n642\t- Upload scoped transcript for unsynced checkpoints\n643\t- `analysis_cache` with freshness, content hash, `(checkpoint_id, repo_id)` binding\n644\t- Verify API responses match requested checkpoint and repo\n645\t- Lesson extractor + preset admission gate\n646\t- Generic-record rejection\n647\t- Ingress sanitization\n648\t- Degraded-mode handling when API is unreachable\n649\t\n650\t### PR 4 — Lesson injection + scoring\n651\t\n652\t- Structured-field scoring engine\n653\t- Embeddings in `balanced`; silent fallback with metrics\n654\t- Outcome bonus, cooldown, diversity\n655\t- TurnStart hook in `off` and `auto` modes\n656\t- Injection logs\n657\t- Latency instrumentation with 50 ms warning\n658\t\n659\t### PR 5 — Shared repo sync (lessons)\n660\t\n661\t- Implement code-owner-selected backend (checkpoint branch or EntireDB)\n662\t- Sync repo-scoped lessons\n663\t- Preserve local-first reads\n664\t- Explicit conflict handling\n665\t\n666\t### PR 6 — TUI review (lessons)\n667\t\n668\t- Candidate review queue\n669\t- Structured field display before promotion\n670\t- Promote / suppress / archive actions\n671\t\n672\t### PR 7 — Experience generation\n673\t\n674\t- Ordered-trajectory source (API extension preferred, local transcript reader as fallback)\n675\t- **Transcript ingress redactor with planted-secret corpus test**\n676\t- Experience extractor + preset admission gate\n677\t- Sanitization + `sanitizer_warnings_json` recording\n678\t- Dedup via experience fingerprint\n679\t- Refresh reports `skipped_no_trajectory_data`\n680\t- All generated experiences enter as `candidate`\n681\t\n682\t### PR 8 — TUI review (experiences)\n683\t\n684\t- Experience list + detail\n685\t- **Rendered-injection-form view** (required for promotion)\n686\t- Surface `sanitizer_warnings_json`\n687\t- Cross-links to related lessons\n688\t\n689\t### PR 9 — Procedural-need classifier + shadow retrieval\n690\t\n691\t- Procedural-need classifier (no new LLM calls)\n692\t- Experience retrieval scorer\n693\t- **Shadow mode**: run retrieval and log selections but do not inject\n694\t- Latency instrumentation for experience retrieval on TurnStart\n695\t- `settings.ExperienceMemoryEnabled` feature flag (default off)\n696\t\n697\t### PR 10 — Experience injection (cohort)\n698\t\n699\t- Flip `settings.ExperienceMemoryEnabled` on for an opt-in cohort\n700\t- **Auto-promotion seed**: apply the quality score from Section 6; mark results `origin = 'generated_auto_promoted'`\n701\t- Lesson/experience conflict suppression (task_class or ≥50% file overlap)\n702\t- Delimited injection template\n703\t- Runtime circuit breaker on SLO violation with `entire status` surface\n704\t- **Success criteria**: at least 5 experience injections per active cohort user per week; no regression on the pre-registered analysis plan; kill switch demonstrably restores lesson-only\n705\t\n706\t### PR 11 — Unified outcome tracking\n707\t\n708\t- `outcome` derivation for both types from `source_signal`\n709\t- `reinforced` / `ineffective` / `neutral`\n710\t- Feed outcomes into scoring\n711\t- Pre-registered analysis plan for the experience default-flip decision\n712\t\n713\t### PR 12 — Derive lessons from experiences\n714\t\n715\t- Derivation job with evidence-independence gate\n716\t- Code-pinned thresholds; settings can raise only\n717\t- Circular-support check keyed on session turn timestamps\n718\t- Per-attempt audit log\n719\t- Derived lessons enter as `candidate` with `source_experience_ids[]`\n720\t- TUI cross-links\n721\t- **Test**: attempting to lower any threshold below its floor is rejected\n722\t- **Test**: a single user with 3 sessions on the same branch does not trigger derivation\n723\t\n724\t---\n725\t\n726\t## 11. Open Questions\n727\t\n728\t1. **Shared repo backend** — checkpoint branch vs EntireDB? Affects PR 5 complexity and long-term audit model.\n729\t2. **What remote state syncs for lessons** — active only, or active + suppressed/archived/history? Affects governance fidelity across users.\n730\t3. **Ordered-trajectory source** — commit to extending `CheckpointAnalysis` with ordered action summaries, or ship the local transcript reader as the permanent solution?\n731\t4. **Experience sync** — when does procedural memory become eligible for repo-scoped sync? Requires a redaction design separate from this doc.\n732\t5. **Manual experience authoring in beta** — allow it behind the `candidate` default, or restrict manual input to lessons until experience quality is established?\n733\t6. **Playbook layer** — the prior experience-layering doc anticipated a future episode-cluster-to-playbook step. When does that earn its way onto the roadmap?\n734\t\n735\t---\n736\t\n737\t## 12. Verification\n738\t\n739\tPer-PR tests are listed in the rollout section. System-level verification to run before the beta default flip:\n740\t\n741\t- Concurrent access: refresh during active session injection causes no data loss\n742\t- Injection latency: measured under realistic memory volume, including experience layer\n743\t- Embedding fallback: correctly recorded in metrics without in-turn warnings\n744\t- Branch cleanup safety: branch memories for branches active in another worktree are preserved\n745\t- Shared repo sync: conflict behavior is explicit and deterministic\n746\t- Outcome derivation: based on source friction signal, not text overlap\n747\t- Secret redaction: planted-secret corpus produces zero egress\n748\t- API availability: refresh degrades gracefully to stale cache\n749\t- Kill switch: reverts to lesson-only within one turn\n750\t- Canary E2E: full flow exercised through Vogon where practical\n751\t"}]},"uuid":"ea67a3d6-25b6-4d61-90b7-908fab7f26bc","timestamp":"2026-04-28T21:35:08.141Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/alisha/.superset/worktrees/cli/agent-improvements/docs/plans/2026-04-16-agent-memory-design.md","content":"  - Friction signal disappears → `reinforced`\n  - Friction signal persists → `ineffective`\n  - Data insufficient → `neutral`\n\n### Gate signals\n\nOutcome tracking feeds two decisions:\n\n1. **Scoring** — outcome bonus/penalty influences future retrieval.\n2. **Default flip** — the experience layer's default switches from off to on only when outcome telemetry meets a pre-registered analysis plan, not just \"session reached a successful stop state.\"\n\n### Pre-registered analysis plan (PR 10 → PR 11 gate)\n\nBefore enabling the experience layer by default, compare on paired session groups (same `source_signal`, same file-dependency profile):\n\n- Time-to-resolution\n- Count of follow-up failures in the same error-signature family within 7 days\n- Count of subsequent user prompts re-asking the same question\n- Minimum injection volume met (≥ 5 experience injections per active cohort user per week)\n\n\"Session reached a successful stop state\" is a crash-regression guardrail, not a benefit signal.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Prompt Injection Hardening\n\nMemory content flows from agent transcripts into future agent prompts. That crosses a data-to-instructions boundary. Controls at every step:\n\n- **Ingress sanitization** — strip role markers, fenced instruction blocks, system-prompt-shaped tag openers, and imperative-plus-verb patterns from every LLM-generated string before storage.\n- **Transcript redaction** — secrets stripped locally before transcript content en